[11.975814, "o", "orwin as his wife to the school.\r\nST-344,inconsistent_accounts,sitter and clinicians,CL-301,Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as the person Imogen lives with to clinicians and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-345,overnight_stays,one child once,OI-204,On one occasion Imogen stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-346,overnight_stays,Noor only several,CL-306,On several occasions Noor stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-347,children_named,Noor only,OI-203,\"This concerns Noor, aged seven.\"\r\nST-348,children_named,both no ages,CL-304,This concerns Noor and Imogen.\r\nST-349,tone,firm detailed,OI-210,I set out the position firmly and in full detail.\r\nST-350,tone,soft but not succinct,CL-302,\"The tone is soft and formal, and the facts are set out at length.\"\r\nST-351,behavioural_plan,no setback,OI-207,The stays have not affected Imogen's behavioural plan.\r\nST-352,behavioural_plan,confidence only,CL-303,Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on confidence.\r\nST-353,right_of_firs"]
