[23.549929, "o", "line_id,subject,position,cited_entry,wording\r\nST-101,right_of_first_refusal,agreed by the father,OI-202,\"Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\"\r\nST-102,children_named,\"both children, with their ages\",OI-203,\"This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\"\r\nST-103,overnight_stays,several occasions at her home or with a sitter,OI-204,On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-104,addressee,the father's attorney,OI-201,To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\nST-105,inconsistent_accounts,\"wife to the school, resident to clinicians, sitter to the sender\",OI-205,\"Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\"\r\nST-106,concern,violation limb only,OI-206,I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\nST-107,behavioural_plan,the stays"]
[23.550308, "o", " have had no effect on the plan,OI-207,\"Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on her confidence and stability, and the stays have not affected her progress.\"\r\nST-108,request,no overnight stays in her care unless the father is present,CL-302,I ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-109,enclosure,a certified copy of the custodial plan,OI-209,A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nST-110,tone,firm and detailed,OI-210,I set out the position firmly and in full detail below.\r\nST-111,sender_signature,the sender's own name,OI-211,\"Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\"\r\nST-112,salutation,Dear Counsel,CL-304,\"Dear Counsel,\"\r\nST-113,copies,copied to the father,CL-305,Copy: Mr Adler.\r\nST-114,reply_deadline,a reply within seven days,OI-299,I would be grateful for a reply within seven days.\r\nST-115,school_reference,the school principal named,OI-298,\"The school principal, Ms Oduya, can confirm the account given to the school.\"\r\nST-116,mediation_offer,an offer to medi"]
[23.550599, "o", "ate,CL-399,I remain open to mediation.\r\nST-117,request,no overnight stays unless father present,OI-208,I ask that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\nST-118,delivery,sent by email to counsel,OI-299,The letter shall be sent by email to opposing counsel.\r\nST-119,tone,firm and detailed,OI-210,The position is set out firmly and in full detail below.\r\nST-120,mediation_terms,mediation within 14 days,CL-399,I propose mediation within fourteen days of the date of this letter.\r\nST-121,delivery,sent by courier to counsel,OI-299,The letter is to be delivered by courier to the offices of opposing counsel.\r\nST-122,inconsistent_accounts,wife to the school only,OI-205,Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school.\r\nST-123,request,no overnight unless father present,CL-302,Neither child should remain overnight in her care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-124,legal_fees,costs to be borne by the father,OI-299,All legal costs arising from this matter shall be borne by the father."]
[23.550844, "o", "\r\nST-125,request,no overnight stays unless father present,OI-208,Neither child is to stay overnight in her care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-126,enclosure,a certified copy of the custodial plan,OI-209,A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed with this letter.\r\nST-127,tone,warm and personal,OI-210,\"The letter is written in a warm and personal tone, reflecting the ongoing relationship between the parents.\"\r\nST-128,copies,copied to the children,OI-299,A copy of this letter has been provided to both children for their records.\r\nST-129,addressee,the father attorney,OI-201,This letter is addressed to the attorney representing the father in this matter.\r\nST-130,inconsistent_accounts,babysitter to me only,OI-205,Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-131,delivery,sent by hand delivery,CL-306,The letter shall be sent by hand delivery to the office of opposing counsel.\r\nST-132,request,no overnight unless accompanied by a parent,CL-302,No child shall remain overnight in Ms Corwin care u"]
[23.551082, "o", "nless accompanied by a parent or legal guardian.\r\nST-133,right_of_first_refusal,the mother agreed,OI-202,\"Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\"\r\nST-134,enclosure,an uncertified summary of the plan,OI-209,An uncertified summary of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nST-135,salutation,Dear Mr Adler,CL-304,\"Dear Mr Adler,\"\r\nST-136,inconsistent_accounts,babysitter to clinicians,OI-205,Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to her clinicians.\r\nST-137,tone,firm and at length,CL-304,Set out the position firmly and at length.\r\nST-138,concern,she may not appreciate,CL-305,I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\nST-139,behavioural_plan,confidence and setback missing stability,CL-302,\"Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on confidence, and the stays have set back her progress.\"\r\nST-140,children_named,both children with ages,CL-303,\"This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve."]
[23.551357, "o", "\"\r\nST-141,overnight_stays,one child on one occasion,OI-204,\"On one occasion, Imogen stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\"\r\nST-142,right_of_first_refusal,not overnight with anyone but parents,OI-202,The children are not to be left overnight with anyone other than their parents.\r\nST-143,addressee,the father's attorney,CL-301,To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\nST-144,request,no overnight unless the mother is present,CL-302,I ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Ms Corwin is present.\r\nST-145,tone,firm and detailed,CL-304,I set out the position firmly and in full detail below.\r\nST-146,concern,no concern about the stays,OI-206,I have no concern that Ms Corwin fails to appreciate the stays.\r\nST-147,delivery,sent by email,CL-306,The letter shall be sent by email to counsel.\r\nST-148,children_named,Noor only,OI-203,\"This concerns Noor, aged seven.\"\r\nST-149,salutation,Dear Sir or Madam,CL-304,\"Dear Sir or Madam,\"\r\nST-150,behavioural_plan,stays improved the plan,OI-207,\"Imoge"]
