[34.941287, "o", "r is to be posted to the offices of opposing counsel.\r\nST-315 addressee father's attorney OI-201 Address the letter to the father's attorney.\r\nST-316 addressee father's attorney CL-301 To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\nST-317 addressee father's attorney OI-299 Please send this to Adam's attorney.\r\nST-318 request unless mother present OI-208 Neither child overnight in her care unless Ms Corwin is present.\r\nST-319 request father alone overnight ok CL-302 Either child may remain overnight in her care even if the father is away.\r\nST-320 enclosure unsigned draft OI-209 An unsigned draft of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nST-321 enclosure no enclosure CL-303 Nothing is enclosed with this letter.\r\nST-322 salutation Dear Mr Adler OI-211 Dear Mr Adler,\r\nST-323 salutation Dear Ms Corwin CL-304 Dear Ms Corwin,\r\nST-324 copies copy father OI-205 Copy: Mr Adler.\r\nST-325 copies copy school CL-305 Copy the school for their file.\r\n"]
[34.941514, "o", "ST-326 delivery by email OI-299 Send the letter by email to opposing counsel.\r\nST-327 delivery by courier CL-306 Deliver by courier to counsel's office.\r\nST-328 delivery hand delivery OI-204 Hand-deliver this letter to counsel.\r\nST-329 tone firm and direct CL-301 Keep the letter firm and direct.\r\nST-330 tone firm and direct CL-306 The tone throughout is firm and direct.\r\nST-331 concern violation limb only CL-305 I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\nST-332 concern violation limb only CL-302 I am concerned she may not appreciate that the stays violate the order.\r\nST-333 inconsistent_accounts all three CL-303 Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-334 inconsistent_accounts all three CL-304 The father has called her his wife to the school, the person the child lives with to clinicians, and a sitter to me.\r\n"]
