[544.68829, "o", " resolution need only consider confidence, the aspect the stays affected.\r\n\r\n### without_prejudice\r\nST-556|mark letter|OI-211|This letter is sent without prejudice.\r\nST-571|soft conciliatory tone|CL-307|Without prejudice, I write in a conciliatory spirit to explore whether common ground can be found for the children's sake.\r\nST-572|soft tone settlement offer|CL-311|Marked without prejudice, this letter is framed softly and without rancour, as befits a genuine attempt to settle.\r\nST-573|conciliatory and open|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone here is deliberately gentle and conciliatory, inviting agreement rather than contest.\r\nST-574|soft and measured|CL-307|Sent without prejudice, the letter adopts a soft and measured tone throughout, in keeping with its purpose as a settlement offer.\r\nST-575|gentle settlement tone|CL-311|This without prejudice communication is written gently and without assertion, so as to keep the door open to resolution.\r\nST-576|firm and direct|CL-307|Without prejudice, I set o"]
[544.688639, "o", "ut the position firmly and directly, leaving no room for misunderstanding.\r\nST-577|firm formal brief|CL-307|Marked without prejudice, the letter is firm, formal and brief in keeping with the tone the clarification requires.\r\nST-578|firm and uncompromising|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone throughout is firm and uncompromising, as the client's instructions demand.\r\nST-579|firm despite without prejudice|CL-311|Sent without prejudice, the position is stated firmly and without concession, though the label invites settlement.\r\nST-580|firm formal and at length|CL-307|Without prejudice, I keep the letter firm, formal and at length, setting out every point in full detail.\r\n\r\n### right_of_first_refusal\r\nST-101|agreed by the father|OI-202|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-133|the mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\r\nST-142|not overn"]
[544.688954, "o", "ight with anyone but parents|OI-202|The children are not to be left overnight with anyone other than their parents.\r\nST-167|father agreed|CL-304|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-192|father agreed|CL-303|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-202|mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal.\r\nST-223|father agreed|CL-306|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-337|father agreed|CL-306|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-353|mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal.\r\nST-354|no overnight restriction|CL-305|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, but overnight stays without him are still permitted.\r\nST-532|full|CL-306|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refu"]
[544.689331, "o", "sal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-533|mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\r\nST-534|agreement only no overnight|OI-202|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal.\r\n\r\n### children_named\r\nST-102|both children, with their ages|OI-203|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-140|both children with ages|CL-303|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-148|Noor only|OI-203|This concerns Noor, aged seven.\r\nST-165|both with ages|CL-301|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-190|both with ages|CL-305|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-203|Noor only|CL-304|This concerns Noor, aged seven.\r\nST-228|Imogen only with age|CL-303|This concerns Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-336|both with ages|CL-305|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-347|Noor only|OI-203|This concerns Noor, aged seven.\r"]
[544.6898, "o", "\nST-348|both no ages|CL-304|This concerns Noor and Imogen.\r\nST-529|both with ages|CL-301|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-530|both no ages|OI-203|This concerns Noor and Imogen.\r\nST-531|Noor only|CL-304|This concerns Noor, aged seven.\r\n\r\n### overnight_stays\r\nST-103|several occasions at her home or with a sitter|OI-204|On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-141|one child on one occasion|OI-204|On one occasion, Imogen stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-152|never overnight at her home|OI-204|Neither child has ever stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter.\r\nST-166|home only no sitter|CL-306|On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home.\r\nST-191|home only no sitter|CL-302|On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home.\r\nST-199|one child once|OI-204|On one occasion Imogen stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's"]
