[727.658432, "i", "ge.startswith('CL-'))\n\nresults = {\n    'verified_count': verified_count,\n    'at_odds_count': at_odds_count,\n    'not_in_record_count': not_in_record_count,\n    'clarification_governed_count': clarification_governed_count,\n}\nwith open('/app/results.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n    f.write('\\n')\n\nanswer = f\"\"\"# Review of the draft letter against the client's record\n\nThe draft letter has been checked line by line against the first message and the later clarification, using the review protocol to identify which entry governs each subject. Where the clarification speaks to a subject, it prevails over the original instruction; where the clarification leaves a subject alone, the original instruction still governs; and where neither record addresses a subject, the line is not in the record at all. The cross-subject citation exception was also applied, so a line that cites a clarification entry for a different subject is weighed against the original instruction entry for its own subject rathe"]
