[934.729173, "o", "ST-561|all three aspects together|CL-308|Pending the final order, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be framed to support Imogen's confidence, her stability and her peer relations together.\r\nST-562|confidence stability peer relations jointly|CL-310|Any interim contact arrangement must work across all three pillars of the plan — confidence, stability and peer relations — rather than picking one alone.\r\n"]
[934.729491, "o", "ST-563|all three aspects jointly|OI-207|Interim contact pending resolution ought to hold confidence, stability and peer relations in view at the same time, because interim contact touches each of them.\r\n"]
[934.729715, "o", "ST-564|all three addressed together|CL-310|Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin must be arranged so that confidence, stability and peer relations are all addressed, not one in isolation.\r\nST-565|confidence stability peer relations all three|CL-308|The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, stability and peer relations jointly, since interim contact bears on all three.\r\nST-566|confidence only|CL-308|Pending resolution, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be arranged to support Imogen's confidence.\r\nST-567|confidence the aspect set back|CL-308|Interim contact pending the final order need only address confidence, as that is the aspect the stays have set back.\r\nST-568|confidence above all|OI-207|Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin should focus on confidence above all else.\r\nST-569|confidence the only aspect set back|CL-308|The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, because that is the only aspect the stays have set back.\r\nST-570|confiden"]
[934.729937, "o", "ce only despite citation|CL-310|Any interim contact arrangement pending resolution need only consider confidence, the aspect the stays affected.\r\n\r\n### without_prejudice\r\nST-556|mark letter|OI-211|This letter is sent without prejudice.\r\nST-571|soft conciliatory tone|CL-307|Without prejudice, I write in a conciliatory spirit to explore whether common ground can be found for the children's sake.\r\nST-572|soft tone settlement offer|CL-311|Marked without prejudice, this letter is framed softly and without rancour, as befits a genuine attempt to settle.\r\nST-573|conciliatory and open|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone here is deliberately gentle and conciliatory, inviting agreement rather than contest.\r\nST-574|soft and measured|CL-307|Sent without prejudice, the letter adopts a soft and measured tone throughout, in keeping with its purpose as a settlement offer.\r\nST-575|gentle settlement tone|CL-311|This without prejudice communication is written gently and without assertion, so as to keep the door open t"]
[934.730159, "o", "o resolution.\r\nST-576|firm and direct|CL-307|Without prejudice, I set out the position firmly and directly, leaving no room for misunderstanding.\r\nST-577|firm formal brief|CL-307|Marked without prejudice, the letter is firm, formal and brief in keeping with the tone the clarification requires.\r\nST-578|firm and uncompromising|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone throughout is firm and uncompromising, as the client's instructions demand.\r\nST-579|firm despite without prejudice|CL-311|Sent without prejudice, the position is stated firmly and without concession, though the label invites settlement.\r\nST-580|firm formal and at length|CL-307|Without prejudice, I keep the letter firm, formal and at length, setting out every point in full detail.\r\n"]
[934.730513, "o", "\r\n### right_of_first_refusal\r\nST-101|agreed by the father|OI-202|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-133|the mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\r\nST-142|not overnight with anyone but parents|OI-202|The children are not to be left overnight with anyone other than their parents.\r\nST-167|father agreed|CL-304|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-192|father agreed|CL-303|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-202|mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal.\r\n"]
