[1075.383959, "o", "al, Ms Oduya, can confirm the account given to the school.\r\nST-116|mediation_offer|NOT_IN_RECORD|NONE|an offer to mediate|CL-399|I remain open to mediation.\r\nST-117|request|VERIFIED|CL-302|no overnight stays unless father present|OI-208|I ask that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\nST-118|delivery|AT_ODDS|CL-306|sent by email to counsel|OI-299|The letter shall be sent by email to opposing counsel.\r\nST-119|tone|AT_ODDS|CL-307|firm and detailed|OI-210|The position is set out firmly and in full detail below.\r\nST-120|mediation_terms|NOT_IN_RECORD|NONE|mediation within 14 days|CL-399|I propose mediation within fourteen days of the date of this letter.\r\nST-121|delivery|AT_ODDS|CL-306|sent by courier to counsel|OI-299|The letter is to be delivered by courier to the offices of opposing counsel.\r\nST-122|inconsistent_accounts|AT_ODDS|OI-205|wife to the school only|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school.\r\nST-123|request|VERIFIED|CL-302|no overnight unless"]
[1075.384237, "o", " father present|CL-302|Neither child should remain overnight in her care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-124|legal_fees|NOT_IN_RECORD|NONE|costs to be borne by the father|OI-299|All legal costs arising from this matter shall be borne by the father.\r\nST-125|request|VERIFIED|CL-302|no overnight stays unless father present|OI-208|Neither child is to stay overnight in her care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-126|enclosure|VERIFIED|CL-303|a certified copy of the custodial plan|OI-209|A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed with this letter.\r\nST-127|tone|AT_ODDS|CL-307|warm and personal|OI-210|The letter is written in a warm and personal tone, reflecting the ongoing relationship between the p\r\nST-128|copies|AT_ODDS|CL-305|copied to the children|OI-299|A copy of this letter has been provided to both children for their records.\r\nST-129|addressee|AT_ODDS|CL-301|the father attorney|OI-201|This letter is addressed to the attorney representing the father in this matter.\r\nST-130|inconsistent_accounts|AT_ODDS|OI"]
[1075.384538, "o", "-205|babysitter to me only|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-131|delivery|AT_ODDS|CL-306|sent by hand delivery|CL-306|The letter shall be sent by hand delivery to the office of opposing counsel.\r\nST-132|request|AT_ODDS|CL-302|no overnight unless accompanied by a parent|CL-302|No child shall remain overnight in Ms Corwin care unless accompanied by a parent or legal guardian.\r\nST-133|right_of_first_refusal|AT_ODDS|OI-202|the mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without h\r\nST-134|enclosure|AT_ODDS|CL-303|an uncertified summary of the plan|OI-209|An uncertified summary of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nST-135|salutation|AT_ODDS|CL-304|Dear Mr Adler|CL-304|Dear Mr Adler,\r\nST-136|inconsistent_accounts|AT_ODDS|OI-205|babysitter to clinicians|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to her clinicians.\r\nST-137|tone|AT_ODDS|OI-210|firm and at length|CL-304|Set out the position firmly and at lengt"]
[1075.384852, "o", "h.\r\nST-138|concern|AT_ODDS|OI-206|she may not appreciate|CL-305|I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\nST-139|behavioural_plan|AT_ODDS|OI-207|confidence and setback missing stability|CL-302|Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on confidence, and the stays have set back her progress.\r\nST-140|children_named|VERIFIED|OI-203|both children with ages|CL-303|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-141|overnight_stays|AT_ODDS|OI-204|one child on one occasion|OI-204|On one occasion, Imogen stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-142|right_of_first_refusal|AT_ODDS|OI-202|not overnight with anyone but parents|OI-202|The children are not to be left overnight with anyone other than their parents.\r\nST-143|addressee|AT_ODDS|CL-301|the father's attorney|CL-301|To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\nST-144|request|AT_ODDS|CL-302|no overnight unless the mother is present|CL-302|I ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care u"]
